    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining current positions without adding or trimming. AMZN trades above all major moving averages (10 EMA $176.74, 50 SMA $168.44, 200 SMA $144.46) in a confirmed uptrend with strong operating cash flow ($84.9B) and a fortress balance sheet. However, the MACD has fallen 44% from its March 4 peak ($4.41 to $2.49) while price sits near highs, RSI shows a bearish divergence (peaked at 68.1 on March 1, now declining), and volume on the latest session was only 0.74x the 20-day average \u2014 all signaling deteriorating momentum near the $181.42 resistance and upper Bollinger Band ($179.95). The risk-reward is asymmetric: ~$10 downside to the 50 SMA versus only $2-3 upside to the range high. Neither a pullback entry toward the 10 EMA/middle Bollinger Band nor a volume-confirmed breakout above $181.42 has materialized, so the disciplined action is to hold at benchmark weight and wait for a clearer signal.\n\n**Entry Price**: 176.74\n\n**Stop Loss**: 168.44\n\n**Position Sizing**: Benchmark or slightly below benchmark weight; do not overweight until breakout above $181.42 on volume or fundamental visibility improves.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
